(1843978, 250072, 29269, '<td valign="top">Great catch! Unfortunately, the nature works in such a way to protect the animals, so their tones blend with the surroundings. That is the only negative that makes this photograph less than superb.</td>', 'Great catch! Unfortunately, the nature works in such a way to protect the animals, so their tones blend with the surroundings. That is the only negative that makes this photograph less than superb.', '2005-11-07 02:08:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1843985, 251473, 29269, '<td valign="top">Beautiful! One of better waterfalls/waterflows in the challenge. The composition is excellent. The only thing I may recommend is showing where the water comes from - the very top-right corner of the photo has the water falling from the sky and perhaps showing another ~50 pixels (in current resolution) would have been better.</td>', 'Beautiful! One of better waterfalls/waterflows in the challenge. The composition is excellent. The only thing I may recommend is showing where the water comes from - the very top-right corner of the photo has the water falling from the sky and perhaps showing another ~50 pixels (in current resolution) would have been better.', '2005-11-07 02:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1843988, 251411, 29269, '<td valign="top">Aah, the randomizer left the best images for last! Iam so glad I went through all the images! And, the inevitable comment - where is the top of his head? It would have been OK to cut him off if there was e.g. a goal in the frame or something more interesting, but this way it''s really missing. Still, 7.</td>', 'Aah, the randomizer left the best images for last! Iam so glad I went through all the images! And, the inevitable comment - where is the top of his head? It would have been OK to cut him off if there was e.g. a goal in the frame or something more interesting, but this way it''s really missing. Still, 7.', '2005-11-07 02:14:11.000000', NULL, 1),
