(1850539, 252332, 35044, '<td valign="top">Excellent GTG picture - nicely composed (Jean has a similarly composed shot that I really like).</td>', 'Excellent GTG picture - nicely composed (Jean has a similarly composed shot that I really like).', '2005-11-09 11:10:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850625, 251716, 14476, '<td valign="top">I too like this image and gave it a six.  <br/> <br/>But that border is a bit difficult for the picture.  I immediately went to the top edges and wondered "whoops, what happened here - should have cropped that..." as the white border appeared to almost blend into the very nice sky. Without that border, I think the image would have placed higher.<br/> <br/>Still, it''s a lovely photograph.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'I too like this image and gave it a six.   But that border is a bit difficult for the picture.  I immediately went to the top edges and wondered "whoops, what happened here - should have cropped that..." as the white border appeared to almost blend into the very nice sky. Without that border, I think the image would have placed higher. Still, it''s a lovely photograph. Alice', '2005-11-09 11:29:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850650, 251716, 40386, '<td valign="top">I agree that the white border makes the sky look blown out, without it I think the pink of the sky would have been great.  The other thing that I dont think helped the shot is the fact that although the water needed to be blurred, the rocks are also soft.<br/> <br/>Edit to add:<br/> <br/>Perhaps a tad more contrast would have helped the sky and rocks?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-09 11:37:42.</i></td>', 'I agree that the white border makes the sky look blown out, without it I think the pink of the sky would have been great.  The other thing that I dont think helped the shot is the fact that although the water needed to be blurred, the rocks are also soft. Edit to add: Perhaps a tad more contrast would have helped the sky and rocks?', '2005-11-09 11:36:59.000000', '2005-11-09 11:37:42.000000', 0),
(1850721, 251987, 46448, '<td valign="top">Hiya Brad,<br/> <br/>I voted this a 5, I thought it met the challenge. Its a good photo but for me it just lacks alot of interest. I feel its a little heavy on the right side with amount of birds. HTH</td>', 'Hiya Brad, I voted this a 5, I thought it met the challenge. Its a good photo but for me it just lacks alot of interest. I feel its a little heavy on the right side with amount of birds. HTH', '2005-11-09 11:59:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850723, 251987, 19708, '<td valign="top">Thanks Jason.<br/>When I first read through that and saw <i>I realize that with a lot of my entries. And that was largely due to your words</i> I gasped for a second.  Then realized it was a compliment, not a blame - LOL.<br/> <br/>The Tamron? I would be happy if it were twice the price.<br/>AF times are fast, it''s quiet and a very sharp piece of glass.</td>', 'Thanks Jason.When I first read through that and saw I realize that with a lot of my entries. And that was largely due to your words I gasped for a second.  Then realized it was a compliment, not a blame - LOL. The Tamron? I would be happy if it were twice the price.AF times are fast, it''s quiet and a very sharp piece of glass.', '2005-11-09 12:00:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850726, 252504, 44924, '<td valign="top">Yes, great shot Rikki, I still think it should have been a ribbon winner though.</td>', 'Yes, great shot Rikki, I still think it should have been a ribbon winner though.', '2005-11-09 12:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850785, 252504, 46651, '<td valign="top">This is still an awesome shot by far. It was refreshing to see this type of image along with a couple of others similar to this instead of the regular "DPC type" images. After reading your setup, kudos to you for trying and having the patience (and your model) to setup this shot. Thanks for the lesson as well. I need to learn this trick. I would have pegged this image in the top 10 and not in the third tier as you find yourself right now. Chin up! This is a great image that is sure to grace your profile page for the next few months. You have a wonderful portfolio of images and I''m sure it wouldn''t take long before you finally get that coveted ribbon.</td>', 'This is still an awesome shot by far. It was refreshing to see this type of image along with a couple of others similar to this instead of the regular "DPC type" images. After reading your setup, kudos to you for trying and having the patience (and your model) to setup this shot. Thanks for the lesson as well. I need to learn this trick. I would have pegged this image in the top 10 and not in the third tier as you find yourself right now. Chin up! This is a great image that is sure to grace your profile page for the next few months. You have a wonderful portfolio of images and I''m sure it wouldn''t take long before you finally get that coveted ribbon.', '2005-11-09 12:09:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850827, 251838, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue with this gorgeous image! Beautifull work!</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue with this gorgeous image! Beautifull work!', '2005-11-09 12:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850833, 252167, 3569, '<td valign="top">I was away for a week and didn''t vote.  This shot definitely deserves a ribbon.  Wonderful in all ways.</td>', 'I was away for a week and didn''t vote.  This shot definitely deserves a ribbon.  Wonderful in all ways.', '2005-11-09 12:24:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850837, 251987, 30861, '<td valign="top">Yo, Brad. I was checking this out due to your posting of your score in a thread, and thought I''d add an observation: you say "4.207 ?? That says to me it did not meet the challenge. I am confused."<br/> <br/>I don''t agree; I think this was seen by most as meeting the challenge, I don''t think that''s an issue here. But it''s a pretty unremarkable picture, in my honest opinion. If you look at the composition organically, it seems muddy and disorganized altogether. It might work better if the brids were sharper, crisper, stood out more, but really it''s just sort of dysfunctional to me. I understand what youw ere after here ''cuz I''ve done a BUNCH of flocking-birds pics in the last few weeks, and not one of them is worth posting up.<br/> <br/>R.</td>', 'Yo, Brad. I was checking this out due to your posting of your score in a thread, and thought I''d add an observation: you say "4.207 ?? That says to me it did not meet the challenge. I am confused." I don''t agree; I think this was seen by most as meeting the challenge, I don''t think that''s an issue here. But it''s a pretty unremarkable picture, in my honest opinion. If you look at the composition organically, it seems muddy and disorganized altogether. It might work better if the brids were sharper, crisper, stood out more, but really it''s just sort of dysfunctional to me. I understand what youw ere after here ''cuz I''ve done a BUNCH of flocking-birds pics in the last few weeks, and not one of them is worth posting up. R.', '2005-11-09 12:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850841, 251987, 36231, '<td valign="top">I really get the feel of the motion in this. It''s really cool.  I just look at, and feel like the birds are moving in front of me. Yes, it is slightly blurred, but that''s what it''s supposed to look like. :)  Definitely was given too low of an overall score.</td>', 'I really get the feel of the motion in this. It''s really cool.  I just look at, and feel like the birds are moving in front of me. Yes, it is slightly blurred, but that''s what it''s supposed to look like. :)  Definitely was given too low of an overall score.', '2005-11-09 12:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850842, 252167, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your Ribbon with this speedy capture! Wow, well done!</td>', 'Congratulations on your Ribbon with this speedy capture! Wow, well done!', '2005-11-09 12:27:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1850846, 251182, 38706, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by json:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by robs:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice timing - So how many eggs did you break? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Like it says in the title, 24 :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Okay - I guess I am one of those types that does not read the title :-))</td>', 'Originally posted by json: Originally posted by robs: Nice timing - So how many eggs did you break?   Like it says in the title, 24 :)   Okay - I guess I am one of those types that does not read the title :-))', '2005-11-09 12:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
