(1860100, 252147, 24500, '<td valign="top">I noticed your post in a forum and was surprised to see such a difficult low light caption with interesting composition and clarity.  The simple fact that you depicted three explosions with seperate charactaristics demonstrates a skillful eye.  The vertical structure is distracting being on a slant towards the right side.  My stereotype of fireworks leaves me hungry for more color.  I did not vote in the shutter speed challenge but you would have gotten a 8 from me.  I have yet to master the ability to take a clear nightime photo.  Good luck and enjoy this site as much as we have.  by Donald</td>', 'I noticed your post in a forum and was surprised to see such a difficult low light caption with interesting composition and clarity.  The simple fact that you depicted three explosions with seperate charactaristics demonstrates a skillful eye.  The vertical structure is distracting being on a slant towards the right side.  My stereotype of fireworks leaves me hungry for more color.  I did not vote in the shutter speed challenge but you would have gotten a 8 from me.  I have yet to master the ability to take a clear nightime photo.  Good luck and enjoy this site as much as we have.  by Donald', '2005-11-12 09:14:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1860341, 251698, 17134, '<td valign="top">Very nice picture but of poor quality. My guess is that the original is very black (maybe 3 to 4 stops underexposed) and you adjusted it so much that it''s visible that you did. Sharpening at this point is, like people commented, a bad idea. The shot should have been made with the shutter open longer than you used now. By doing so it would have qualified better for the challenge (wich is shutter speed).<br/> <br/>Would be nice to see wich shutter speed you used on this (considering it is the shutter speed competition).<br/> <br/>You got a good rating just because the picture in itself is gorgeous, my compliments on that!</td>', 'Very nice picture but of poor quality. My guess is that the original is very black (maybe 3 to 4 stops underexposed) and you adjusted it so much that it''s visible that you did. Sharpening at this point is, like people commented, a bad idea. The shot should have been made with the shutter open longer than you used now. By doing so it would have qualified better for the challenge (wich is shutter speed). Would be nice to see wich shutter speed you used on this (considering it is the shutter speed competition). You got a good rating just because the picture in itself is gorgeous, my compliments on that!', '2005-11-12 12:08:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1860414, 251860, 47508, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Love the scenery and the powerful sensation of the waterfalls. Congratulations!</td>', 'Great shot! Love the scenery and the powerful sensation of the waterfalls. Congratulations!', '2005-11-12 12:37:54.000000', NULL, 0),
